{
  "model": "Flash-energy calibration from events only, version 3 (final review round, F05).\n\nVersion 2 (review round 2, N04) removed the truth onset and record length. Version 3 changes:\n  * range and earthshine are drawn JOINTLY for every flash from the same observing opportunity\n    (version 2 drew one earthshine value per batch, independent of the ranges); flashes are then grouped\n    into 10% background bins for simulation, so the background diversity equals the number of flashes;\n  * mismatch tests are run twice: with thresholds re-derived for the true sensor (an adapted detector)\n    and with the NOMINAL thresholds (an unknown drift that the detector does not know about);\n  * a finite-prehistory test starts every pixel's reference at a random point within one threshold;\n  * a symmetric-BA test splits background activity equally into ON and OFF events (the ON-only\n    surrogate creates a positive decoded drift);\n  * the warm sensor is tested with the nominal correction and with a correction retrained for it;\n  * the condition-dependent bias and scatter of the corrected energy (by decay time and background) are\n    written out for the joint fit (joint_model.py), instead of one Gaussian width.\nThe correction is a quadratic regression of ln(E_true/E_raw) on [ln E_raw, ln active duration, peak\ndecoded level, pixels with events, ln measured background], trained on the nominal sensor with\nexponential profiles. Only detected flashes enter. Writes photometry_calibration.json.\nNot modelled: refractory period, readout saturation, decoder resets during long records.\n",
